      "Fixed: the \u201cvs S&P 500\u201d card was blank on the day of your first trade. It measured the index from your first buy but needed an index price dated that same day, which does not exist until the session closes. It now takes the last close before you bought, so the comparison works from day one. Its return figure was also mixing dollars and euros, reading -1.3% where the truth was -1.1%.",
